{
  "uid": "fleet-batch-reconciliation",
  "title": "Fleet \u00b7 Batch Reconciliation (daily)",
  "description": "The daily half of the business question \u2014 which vehicles are becoming unprofitable once yesterday's fuel and maintenance costs are factored in \u2014 plus the state of the batch/speed boundary that answer depends on.",
  "tags": [
    "fleet",
    "lambda",
    "business",
    "batch"
  ],
  "timezone": "utc",
  "editable": true,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-1h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Which vehicles are becoming unprofitable \u2014 the daily half of the question",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Worst 10 by 7-day rolling average profit",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "yesoreyeram-infinity-datasource",
        "uid": "fleet-api"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "yesoreyeram-infinity-datasource",
            "uid": "fleet-api"
          },
          "type": "json",
          "source": "url",
          "format": "table",
          "url": "/api/v1/vehicles/unprofitable?limit=10",
          "url_options": {
            "method": "GET",
            "data": ""
          },
          "root_selector": "",
          "columns": [
            {
              "selector": "vehicle_id",
              "text": "Vehicle",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "selector": "classification",
              "text": "Class",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "selector": "rolling_7d_avg_profit",
              "text": "7d avg profit",
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "selector": "net_profit",
              "text": "Net profit (day)",
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "selector": "profit_trend_slope",
              "text": "Trend slope",
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "selector": "margin_pct",
              "text": "Margin %",
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "selector": "trips",
              "text": "Trips",
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "selector": "utilization_pct",
              "text": "Utilisation %",
              "type": "number"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "description": "\u2605 The direct answer to the assignment's business question. Ordered by the 7-DAY ROLLING AVERAGE, not by today's profit: the question asks which vehicles are BECOMING unprofitable, and one bad day is noise \u2014 sorting on it would rank a vehicle that had a single long deadhead above one that has lost money every day for a week. Exact figures from the batch view, computed over the immutable master dataset.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "How far the exact answer extends",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Batch watermark age (sim days)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "fleet-prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 11
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "fleet-prom"
          },
          "expr": "max(serving_batch_watermark_age_sim_days)",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "description": "Simulated days between the batch high-water mark and now. 1 is healthy \u2014 yesterday is complete. Climbing means the batch layer has stopped, and that failure has NO other symptom: the speed layer keeps serving, the API keeps answering, and the dashboard stays green while more and more of every query is answered approximately.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 2
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Rows in the batch view",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "yesoreyeram-infinity-datasource",
        "uid": "fleet-api"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 11
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "yesoreyeram-infinity-datasource",
            "uid": "fleet-api"
          },
          "type": "json",
          "source": "url",
          "format": "table",
          "url": "/api/v1/pipeline/status",
          "url_options": {
            "method": "GET",
            "data": ""
          },
          "root_selector": "",
          "columns": [
            {
              "selector": "pnl_rows",
              "text": "P&L rows",
              "type": "number"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "description": "Per-vehicle daily P&L rows in mart.fact_vehicle_daily_pnl. Should be exactly (simulated days processed) x (fleet size). A count that is not a clean multiple of the fleet size means a day was partially processed.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Restated rows",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "yesoreyeram-infinity-datasource",
        "uid": "fleet-api"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 11
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "yesoreyeram-infinity-datasource",
            "uid": "fleet-api"
          },
          "type": "json",
          "source": "url",
          "format": "table",
          "url": "/api/v1/pipeline/status",
          "url_options": {
            "method": "GET",
            "data": ""
          },
          "root_selector": "",
          "columns": [
            {
              "selector": "restated_rows",
              "text": "Restated",
              "type": "number"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "description": "Rows whose value changed after first publication \u2014 a figure an auditor asks about. Re-running the batch layer with the SAME job_run_id leaves this at zero, which is how idempotency is demonstrated; a restatement run with a new id increments it deliberately.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Merge boundary crossings",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "fleet-prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 11
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "fleet-prom"
          },
          "expr": "max(serving_merge_boundary_crossings_total)",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "description": "Requests whose date range spanned the batch/speed boundary, so BOTH views contributed. This is the reconciliation actually happening. A flat zero means every request landed wholly inside one view and the merge \u2014 the thing this architecture is justified by \u2014 was never exercised.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Speed view vs batch view \u2014 Lambda's stated weakness, measured",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Degraded responses /sec by missing store",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "fleet-prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 17
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "fleet-prom"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (missing_store) (rate(serving_degraded_responses_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{missing_store}}",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "description": "Serving partial data with X-Data-Degraded is CORRECT behaviour, so this is not an error counter. A rate sustained above zero means one store is unreachable and the answer is coming from half the architecture \u2014 exact figures gone if it is Postgres, the live view gone if it is Redis.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 12,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {}
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Uncovered dates /sec",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "fleet-prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 17
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "fleet-prom"
          },
          "expr": "rate(serving_uncovered_dates_total[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "dates neither view could answer",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "description": "Requested simulated dates that NEITHER view could answer for. Redis holds only the current window, so when the batch layer falls more than one simulated day behind, the days in between are in no store at all. Returning fewer rows silently would make a lagging pipeline look like a quiet week, so the merge names them in the response instead.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 12,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {}
    }
  ]
}
